**2** **out of the common, extraordinary, strange**, ἔ τι περισσὸν εἰδείη if he has any **signal** knowledge, {{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 769}}; εἴ τι φρονεῖς καί τι περισσὸν ἔχεις Philisc.{{Refs 5th c.BC+|(“PLG” 2.327); π. λόγος 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Tyrannus” 841; ἄγρα 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Bacchae” 1197 (Lyric poetry); πάθος [prev. author] “Supp.” 791 (Lyric poetry); βίος οὐδὲν ἔχων π. ἀλλὰ πάντα σμικρά 5th c.BC: Antipho Sophista 51; οὐ γὰρ π. οὐδὲν οὐδ᾽ ἔξω λόγου πέπονθας 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 437; περισσότερα παθήματα 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 3.4.5; τὰ π. τῶν ἔργων καὶ τερατώδη 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 12.77}}; ἴδια καὶ π. {{Refs 4th c.BC+|[prev. author] 15.145; π. καὶ θαυμαστά 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1141b6}}; πρᾶξις π. {{Refs|[prev. author] “Pol.” 1312a27; οὐθὲν δὴ λέγοντες π. φαίνονταί τι λέγειν [prev. author] “Metaphorical” 1053b3}}; τί π. ποιεῖτ; {{NT+4th c.BC+|NT.Matt.5.47; περιττοτάτη φύσις 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Historia Animalium” 531a9}}; συνανθρωπίζον.. πάντων περισσότατον, of the dog, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|2nd c.AD: Athenaeus Epigrammaticus 13.611c, compare 4th-3rd c.BC: Clearchus Historicus 24}}; in Literature, **striking**, τὸ περιττόν, as a quality of οἱ τοῦ Σωκράτους λόγοι, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1265a11}}; τὰ σοφὰ καὶ τὰ π. **refinements**, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Epicurus Philosophus “Fragmenta” 409}}; opposed to κοινὸς καὶ δημώδης, {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|3rd c.AD: Longinus Rhetor 40.2}} (but also, **elaborate**, π. καὶ πεποιημένος {{Refs|[prev. author] 3.4}}; in bad sense, **far-fetched**, {{Refs 1st c.BC+|1st c.BC: Dionysius Halicarnassensis “Epistula ad Pompeium” 2, “Dem.” 56).}}
